1
00:02:18,071 --> 00:02:20,071
Oh

2
00:02:48,071 --> 00:03:18,031
Has to keep your love coming.

3
00:03:18,031 --> 00:03:42,491
Thank you.

4
00:03:48,031 --> 00:03:55,031
Eternal farewell, Niko Robin, the woman who draws darkness.

5
00:03:55,031 --> 00:04:01,031
We're here! We're here! Come on, Granny! Hurry! Hurry!

6
00:04:01,031 --> 00:04:05,031
Calm down. Get a hold of yourself.

7
00:04:05,031 --> 00:04:11,031
What a seven. It's been a while.

8
00:04:11,031 --> 00:04:13,031
Granny! Hurry! Hurry!

9
00:04:13,031 --> 00:04:15,031
Okay, okay!

10
00:04:15,031 --> 00:04:20,031
Attention all passengers! Wearing a mask on the sea train today is strictly prohibited.

11
00:04:20,031 --> 00:04:23,031
Look, ma'am, just cooperate and show me your face.

12
00:04:23,031 --> 00:04:26,031
This is my face. See?

13
00:04:26,031 --> 00:04:29,031
Huh? Hey, you.

14
00:04:29,031 --> 00:04:32,031
Oh, uh, Miss Kokoro. So nice to see you again.

15
00:04:32,031 --> 00:04:34,031
What's going on here? Trouble?

16
00:04:34,031 --> 00:04:40,031
Yes, yes, ma'am. Everyone is on the lookout for the Straw Hat Pirates, the culprits in the attempted assassination of Iceberg.

17
00:04:40,031 --> 00:04:43,031
Icebergs? Assassins?

18
00:04:43,031 --> 00:04:46,031
What is it, Granny? Huh?

19
00:04:46,031 --> 00:04:48,031
Hey, wait a minute.

20
00:04:48,031 --> 00:04:50,031
Huh?

21
00:04:50,031 --> 00:04:56,031
I'm falling! I'm falling! I'm falling! I'm falling!

22
00:04:56,031 --> 00:04:59,031
I'm falling! I'm falling!

23
00:04:59,031 --> 00:05:03,031
Whoa!

24
00:05:03,031 --> 00:05:05,031
Whoa!

25
00:05:05,031 --> 00:05:07,031
Whoa!

26
00:05:11,031 --> 00:05:14,031
Whew! Good. Safe and sound.

27
00:05:14,031 --> 00:05:16,031
Yeah. That wore me out, huh?

28
00:05:16,031 --> 00:05:20,031
Safe and sound my butt! I thought I was gonna die!

29
00:05:20,031 --> 00:05:26,031
What was I supposed to do? You were the one who said we couldn't use the elevator because we get caught! I didn't have a choice!

30
00:05:27,031 --> 00:05:32,031
That doesn't mean, hey, let's jump down, idiot! You can't glide around like that square-nosed shipwright! Got it?

31
00:05:32,031 --> 00:05:34,031
Right. Sorry about that.

32
00:05:35,031 --> 00:05:37,031
Whatever. It's fine since we're safe now.

33
00:05:37,031 --> 00:05:39,031
Then stop hitting me!

34
00:05:39,031 --> 00:05:45,031
However, we might not be safe for long.

35
00:05:46,031 --> 00:05:48,031
We won't? Why not? What's wrong?

36
00:05:49,031 --> 00:05:57,031
This island's topography and climate. With this much wind blowing and the atmospheric pressure falling so rapidly, there's likely going to be a typhoon here tonight.

37
00:05:57,031 --> 00:06:03,031
This place is called the City of Water. Think about it. Its greatest weakness would have to be flooding.

38
00:06:04,031 --> 00:06:06,031
Okay, so it floods, so what?

39
00:06:06,031 --> 00:06:09,031
Well, it worries me, that's all. I'll check into it later.

40
00:06:10,031 --> 00:06:12,031
Come on, let's head back to the inn for the time being.

41
00:06:27,031 --> 00:06:35,031
Hey there. Welcome. How are ya?

42
00:06:36,031 --> 00:06:38,031
Ow! How's everything going, Bluno?

43
00:06:39,031 --> 00:06:42,031
Feelin' super!

44
00:06:44,031 --> 00:06:46,031
Yeah, well, I suppose you could say that.

45
00:06:47,031 --> 00:06:53,031
What do you mean, suppose? You're not a very decisive guy, are you? I'll take the usual. Fill her up, please!

46
00:06:53,031 --> 00:06:58,031
Do you got any money? Just fill them up, will ya? Cola!

47
00:06:59,031 --> 00:07:03,031
I think you run an establishment like this with the greedy notion of taking money from your customers.

48
00:07:04,031 --> 00:07:05,031
We do have a little money.

49
00:07:06,031 --> 00:07:07,031
About a million berries left from our shopping spree.

50
00:07:08,031 --> 00:07:16,031
What? We have that much left? How disgraceful! How totally uncool to think that I didn't spend it all in one night!

51
00:07:17,031 --> 00:07:18,031
Here, give me that!

52
00:07:19,031 --> 00:07:22,031
Wow! Listen up! This is your lucky day, customers!

53
00:07:22,031 --> 00:07:25,031
All your drinks are on me! Knock back as much booze as you like!

54
00:07:26,031 --> 00:07:28,031
Compliments of me, your pal Frankie!

55
00:07:29,031 --> 00:07:32,031
Yay! That's our Frankie! You're the best!

56
00:07:33,031 --> 00:07:36,031
The face of one or seventh underworld! What a guy!

57
00:07:37,031 --> 00:07:40,031
Whoa! That's awesome! Look over here! It's pal-dum-

58
00:07:41,031 --> 00:07:45,031
So, Bluno, where's my cola? Come on, hurry it up already!

59
00:07:46,031 --> 00:07:48,031
Looks like business has been good for you, Frankie.

60
00:07:48,031 --> 00:07:50,031
Ugh!

61
00:07:51,031 --> 00:07:54,031
Old Hat Kokoro! That was you I sat next to?

62
00:07:55,031 --> 00:07:57,031
I thought it was a statue of a sea monster!

63
00:08:00,031 --> 00:08:03,031
Granny! Is it okay for me to get a refill of my juice then?

64
00:08:04,031 --> 00:08:07,031
Hey kid, this is a bar. It's no place for little shrimps like you!

65
00:08:08,031 --> 00:08:09,031
Business has been good, right?

66
00:08:09,031 --> 00:08:13,031
Ugh! Fine, whatever! Suit yourself!

67
00:08:14,031 --> 00:08:15,031
Hooray! Juice!

68
00:08:16,031 --> 00:08:18,031
Yeah, business has been outstanding, but I feel terrible!

69
00:08:19,031 --> 00:08:21,031
In fact, this entire week has been a total downer!

70
00:08:22,031 --> 00:08:24,031
And it's all because of that stupid pirate!

71
00:08:24,031 --> 00:08:25,031
Here you go, full take!

72
00:08:26,031 --> 00:08:27,031
Good! Took you long enough!

73
00:08:28,031 --> 00:08:30,031
Fuel! Fuel! Fuel! Fuel! Fuel!

74
00:08:30,031 --> 00:08:36,031
Come on, come on, come on, come on, come on!

75
00:08:49,031 --> 00:08:51,031
Super!

76
00:08:52,031 --> 00:08:54,031
There! Completely restored!

77
00:08:55,031 --> 00:08:57,031
That bastard, wait till I get my hands on him!

78
00:08:58,031 --> 00:09:00,031
Hey, Hag! Why are you here?

79
00:09:01,031 --> 00:09:03,031
Aqua Laguna is on its way.

80
00:09:04,031 --> 00:09:07,031
Is that right? No wonder the wind's blowing so strong today.

81
00:09:08,031 --> 00:09:10,031
You need to get your house prepped up for the storm.

82
00:09:11,031 --> 00:09:15,031
Well, there's nothing much to prep really, seeing as how I don't actually have a house anymore.

83
00:09:15,031 --> 00:09:25,031
I was going to have a drink with Iceberg, but it seems he was shot.

84
00:09:26,031 --> 00:09:29,031
Yeah, I heard about that. They say pirates are responsible.

85
00:09:30,031 --> 00:09:32,031
Gallylaw and the townspeople are raging pissed.

86
00:09:33,031 --> 00:09:34,031
So a pirate did it, huh?

87
00:09:35,031 --> 00:09:38,031
Do you honestly think that's what happened?

88
00:09:39,031 --> 00:09:43,031
Hey, you sound like you know something. If you really do, then spit it out, you old hag!

89
00:09:43,031 --> 00:09:47,031
Iceberg's constantly being hounded by the world government. You ever notice that?

90
00:09:48,031 --> 00:09:52,031
So? Wait, are you trying to say that government lapdog Corgi pulled the trigger?

91
00:09:53,031 --> 00:09:56,031
That little troll isn't cut out to try something like that.

92
00:09:56,031 --> 00:10:00,031
You're right. That assassination plot falls more in line with the work of CP9.

93
00:10:01,031 --> 00:10:03,031
Is that right, Bluto? Ever heard of him?

94
00:10:04,031 --> 00:10:05,031
Only rumors, really.

95
00:10:06,031 --> 00:10:11,031
Jeez, you village simpletons sure put a lot of stock into stories about imaginary boogeyman shadow organizations.

96
00:10:11,031 --> 00:10:16,031
Don't be an idiot. Of course they exist. They just never show themselves.

97
00:10:16,031 --> 00:10:19,031
Can't really work undercover if everyone knows who you are.

98
00:10:25,031 --> 00:10:29,031
You seem pretty sure of yourself. Got some kind of proof about this?

99
00:10:30,031 --> 00:10:32,031
Nope, just rumors.

100
00:10:32,031 --> 00:10:37,031
Stop screwing around, hag! Look, rumors are superstitious nonsense!

101
00:10:37,031 --> 00:10:40,031
Strange they've remained a rumor for such a long time, huh?

102
00:10:41,031 --> 00:10:44,031
They're good at eliminating people without anyone noticing.

103
00:10:45,031 --> 00:10:47,031
If you mess with them, you're dead meat.

104
00:10:47,031 --> 00:11:00,031
Impressive work. The assignment we had to do yesterday would very well.

105
00:11:01,031 --> 00:11:03,031
Excellent job, Nico Robin.

106
00:11:03,031 --> 00:11:07,031
Thanks, it was a cakewalk.

107
00:11:08,031 --> 00:11:12,031
Though naturally, you're now being pursued by every last person in the city.

108
00:11:13,031 --> 00:11:14,031
Indeed I am.

109
00:11:15,031 --> 00:11:16,031
Merely a temporary setback.

110
00:11:17,031 --> 00:11:20,031
Tonight is what's important. Understand?

111
00:11:21,031 --> 00:11:24,031
We'll infiltrate Iceberg's residents one more time.

112
00:11:24,031 --> 00:11:29,031
If it becomes a worst case scenario, you're free to eliminate all of the evidence.

113
00:11:30,031 --> 00:11:33,031
Among Tom's apprentices who could have had it from the very beginning,

114
00:11:34,031 --> 00:11:36,031
Iceberg is the only one that remains alive.

115
00:11:37,031 --> 00:11:41,031
No matter how much he denies having it in the name of CP9,

116
00:11:42,031 --> 00:11:43,031
we will take it tonight.

117
00:11:44,031 --> 00:11:47,031
Never forget, this is a mission of justice.

118
00:11:47,031 --> 00:12:11,031
In compliance with the Aqua Laguna warning that was issued for the entire island earlier today,

119
00:12:12,031 --> 00:12:16,031
all docks on the shipbuilding island are now to be considered public shelter and evacuation centers.

120
00:12:17,031 --> 00:12:22,031
Large crowds are expected, so please take shelter as quickly as possible.

121
00:12:23,031 --> 00:12:28,031
Additionally, keep in mind that Dock 1 is currently in a dangerous state.

122
00:12:29,031 --> 00:12:31,031
Alright, I'll put the iron board on.

123
00:12:32,031 --> 00:12:35,031
Hey, honey, you sure we have everything we'll need?

124
00:12:36,031 --> 00:12:38,031
Yes, now come on. We need to take shelter in the shipyard.

125
00:12:39,031 --> 00:12:40,031
Yeah, Dad, let's get going!

126
00:12:41,031 --> 00:12:42,031
Come on, hurry!

127
00:12:43,031 --> 00:12:45,031
Patience, patience. You gotta be careful sealing this board.

128
00:12:45,031 --> 00:12:48,031
If the inside of our house gets flooded, everything will be ruined.

129
00:12:49,031 --> 00:12:51,031
Tie that side down too! Move it!

130
00:12:52,031 --> 00:12:54,031
Hey! The wind is starting to pick up!

131
00:12:55,031 --> 00:12:57,031
The waves will be here anytime now! Hurry!

132
00:12:58,031 --> 00:13:01,031
If we take too long, those assassin pirates are gonna show up too!

133
00:13:02,031 --> 00:13:03,031
What?

134
00:13:03,031 --> 00:13:06,031
Where'd he disappear to? I'm sure he went this way!

135
00:13:07,031 --> 00:13:08,031
He's gotta be around here!

136
00:13:08,031 --> 00:13:10,031
Okay, you guys look over there!

137
00:13:10,031 --> 00:13:11,031
Right!

138
00:13:11,031 --> 00:13:23,031
What the hell is going on? Are they chasing me? I don't understand.

139
00:13:23,031 --> 00:13:34,031
Wait a sec. Is this why everyone's chasing after me?

140
00:13:35,031 --> 00:13:36,031
Culprits in the assassination plot.

141
00:13:37,031 --> 00:13:40,031
Well, that sucks. Can't go back to the inn now. I'll be out in the open.

142
